Installing program.

0: Setup the driver Hat/Bonnet
  If using Adafruit RGB Matrices, on the backside of the bonnet, short the E jumper to 8.
  If using another card, check your documentation, but you may need short the E jumper to 16.

1: Configure the OS settings.
  #Disable WLAN Power Management
  #  sudo /sbin/iwconfig wlan0 power off
  #  add to /etc/rc.local ???

  Disable the sound driver:
    edit /boot/firmware/config.txt
    Add the line:
      dtparam=audio=off

  Blacklist the sound driver (the above is sometimes insufficient):
    edit (or create) /etc/modprobe.d/blacklist-custom.conf
    Add the line:
      blacklist snd_bcm2835
  
  Isolate CPUs
      edit /boot/firmware/cmdline.txt
          Add "isolcpus=3" to the command line
        eg: "console=serial0,115200 console=tty1 root=PARTUUID=c32373bb-02 rootfstype=ext4 fsck.repair=yes rootwait cfg80211.ieee80211_regdom=US isolcpus=3"

  Enable i2c (if using the remote functionality)
      sudo raspi-config
      select Interfaces
      select I2C
      select Enable

2: Install git and some other things
    sudo apt install git i2c-tools python3-pip python3-setuptools
    [sudo apt install procs btop fd-find bat]

3: install uv.   Note, if you get errors about "externally managed environment", add the "--break-system-packages"
  sudo pip install [--break-system-packages] uv

4: Clone flaschen-taschen
  git clone --recursive https://github.com/hzeller/flaschen-taschen.git

5: Build and install ft-server:
  cd flaschen-taschen/server 
  make FT_BACKEND=rgb-matrix
  cp ft-server /usr/local/bin

6: Clone and install LMSDisplay.  Note, if you get errors about "externally managed environment", add the "--break-system-packages"
  git clone REPOSITORY/LMSDisplay
  cd LMSDisplay
  sudo uv pip install --system . [--break-system-packages]

6: Install and start the flaschen taschen service
  cp ft-server.service /usr/lib/systemd/system/
  [ ln -s /usr/lib/systemd/system/ft-server.service /etc/systemd/system/multi-user.target.wants/ ]
  systemctl enable ft-server.service
  systemctl start ft-server.service

  Note: If the screen shows strange behavior, add the switch --led-slowdown-gpio=x where x is a number between 1 and 4.
  1 is the default, 2 seems to work for many screens.   Adjust as needed.
8: Install and start the LMSDisplay services
  # cp lmsdisplay.service lmsconfig.service /usr/lib/systemd/system/
  # [ ln -s /usr/lib/systemd/system/{lmsdisplay,lmsconfig}.service /etc/systemd/system/multi-user.target.wants/ ]
  systemctl enable lmsdisplay.service lmsconfig.service lmsremote.service
  systemctl start lmsdisplay.service lmsconfig.service lmsremote.service

9: Configure the display.
  Use a browser to connect to http://[DISPLAYMACHINE]:5000
  Set, at a minimum, the LMS Server and Player you wish to monitor.
